lesson: 242
title: Canadian coins
level: primary-3
stars: 0
explain: In Canada the one-dollar coin is called a loonie, because it has a loon on it, and the two-dollar coin is called a toonie.
explain: To count the money, each toonie gives 2 dollars and each loonie gives 1 dollar; add the two amounts.
explain: 3 toonies and 2 loonies make 3 × 2 + 2 = 8 dollars.
vars: a=name b=name x=2..12 y=2..12 z=2..9
answer: 2 * x + y
exercise: {a} has {x} toonies and {y} loonies. How many dollars does {a.he} have?
exercise: In {a.his} piggy bank {a} finds {x} toonies and {y} loonies. How much money is that in dollars?
exercise: Grandpa gives {a} {x} toonies, and {a.his} aunt gives {a.him} {y} loonies. How many dollars has {a} got now?
exercise: At a bake sale in Winnipeg, {a} collects {x} toonies and {y} loonies. How many dollars did the bake sale take?
exercise: {a} pays for a book with {x} toonies and {y} loonies and gets no change. How many dollars does the book cost?
exercise: got {x} toonies n {y} loonies in my pocket eh, how many bucks is that
exercise: {a} found {x+1} toonies, no wait {x}, and {y} loonies under the couch. how much money
exercise: {a}'s jar: {x} toonies, {y} loonies, and like a million buttons lol. dollars?
exercise: {b} reckons {x} toonies and {y} loonies is {x+y} dollars. that's not right is it? how many dollars really
exercise: tooth fairy left {a} {x} toonies and {y} loonies, how much in dollars
exercise: {a} saved {x} toonies and {y} loonies for a hockey stick. how many dollars saved
test: How many dollars do {y} loonies and {x} toonies add up to?
test: The tip jar at a café in Halifax holds {y} loonies and {x} toonies. What is the total in dollars?
test: {a} counts {x} toonies; {b} counts {y} loonies and {z} buttons. How many dollars did the two children count together?
test: A parking meter in Toronto took {x} toonies and {y} loonies today. How much money did it take?
test: {a} trades all {a.his} coins, {x} toonies and {y} loonies, for a single note of the same value. What is the note's value in dollars?
test: {y} loonies plus {x} toonies, whats the total eh
test: me n {b} pooled {x} toonies and {y} loonies for pizza, how many dollars we got
exam: Determine the aggregate monetary value, in Canadian dollars, of a collection comprising {x.words} toonies and {y.words} loonies.
exam: It is given that a sum is tendered exclusively in toonies, numbering {x}, and loonies, numbering {y}. State the said sum in dollars.
exam: Ascertain the total sum, expressed in dollars, held by {a}, whose purse is stated to contain {y} loonies together with {x} toonies.
exam: Whereas a collection box is found upon inspection to contain {x} toonies and {y} loonies, compute the value of its contents in dollars.
exercise: {a}'s grandpa, who passed away in the spring, left {a.him} {x} toonies and {y} loonies in an old tin. How many dollars is that?
exercise: {b} borrowed {a}'s piggy bank, nicked it more like, the little thief, and found {x} toonies and {y} loonies inside. how many bucks did the rat take?
test: Before he was let go from the hockey rink, {a}'s uncle had saved {x} toonies and {y} loonies. What are his savings worth in dollars?
